From: NeuroCore OS Contributors <kernel@neurocore-os.org>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] init/version: append NeuroCore OS boot banner marker

Adds a clean NeuroCore OS identification tag to the early boot kernel version
banner so serial console CI checks and support logs distinguish official
NeuroCore LTS/next kernels cleanly.

Signed-off-by: NeuroCore OS Contributors <kernel@neurocore-os.org>
---
 init/version-timestamp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/version-timestamp.c b/init/version-timestamp.c
index 6c0f7c7a0b01..b9d4c23e1a44 100644
--- a/init/version-timestamp.c
+++ b/init/version-timestamp.c
@@ -27,5 +27,5 @@
 
 /* FIXED STRINGS! Don't touch! */
 const char linux_banner[] =
-	"Linux version " UTS_RELEASE " (" LINUX_COMPILE_BY "@"
+	"NeuroCore OS Linux version " UTS_RELEASE " (" LINUX_COMPILE_BY "@"
 	LINUX_COMPILE_HOST ") (" LINUX_COMPILER ") " UTS_VERSION "\n";
-- 
2.47.0
